  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8d835d7a-fe3c-57e7-9de6-f28d9801b883",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ -6x-4y &=6,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system is consistent dependent\n\nIII. The system has no solution",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find the solution to the system. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -4 & 6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n3x+2y=-3\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "852d333d-0f7a-5527-a833-e6f43c70f745",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
