    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5d64775f-feec-547d-a7fd-57d750940e70",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y &=-1 \\\\ 4x-4y &=0 \\\\ 10x-23y &=-16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -23 & -16\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -23 & -16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 10 & -23 & -16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(5){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -18 & -21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is inconsistent.",
