    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f9fdc0f5-9893-564b-8197-6fdf747323cd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-3z &=4 \\\\ x-y-4z &=7 \\\\ -2x+2y+7z &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 7 & -15\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & -7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent independent.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0efc3b78-ee7c-59d2-a78d-830c23afbfba",
          ":answer-field/key": "The system is consistent independent",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
